{title: Holy, Holy, Holy! Lord God Almighty}
{artist: Reginald Heber}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune NICAEA - John B. Dykes (1861)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1826, tune 1861: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
Early in the [Bm]morning our [E]song shall rise to [A]Thee;
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy, [G]merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]Persons, [Em]bless[A]ed Trini[D]ty!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]All the saints a[D]dore Thee,
Casting down their [Bm]golden crowns a[E]round the glassy [A]sea;
[D]Cherubim and [Bm]seraphim [G]falling down be[D]fore Thee,
[G]Which wert, and [D]art, and [Em]ever[A]more shalt [D]be.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]though the darkness [D]hide Thee,
Though the eye of [Bm]sinful man Thy [E]glory may not [A]see;
[D]Only Thou art [Bm]holy; there is [G]none beside [D]Thee,
[G]Perfect in [D]power, in [Em]love, and [A]puri[D]ty.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
All Thy works shall [Bm]praise Thy name, in [E]earth, and sky, and [A]sea;
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy; [G]merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]Persons, [Em]bless[A]ed Trini[D]ty!
{end_of_verse}
